{{!-- A section's title line. Pass `collapse` (the id to remember the fold under)
      to give it a hover fold caret — only where the heading's FOLLOWING SIBLINGS
      are that section's body, which is not true everywhere this partial is used
      (a Lore sub-heading sits inside its own entry box, and the sidebar move
      groups already fold by clicking the heading). Sections that carry an edit
      pencil get their caret from section-edit-toggle instead, so it can sit
      beside the pencil.

      `caret` is the same mark without the button: for a heading that is ITSELF
      the fold control (the Major / Minor arcana sections, where clicking
      anywhere on the line folds it), so the state still reads the same way as
      every other section. Pass one or the other, never both.

      `randomize` is the section key for a "roll one at random" button, sat right
      after the note. Optional like the rest: pass nothing and no button is
      emitted, so every existing caller is untouched. --}}
<h3 class="stonetop-move-group-title">{{title}}{{#if note}} <span class="stonetop-section-note">{{note}}</span>{{/if}}{{#if randomize}} {{> "stonetop.section-randomize" section=randomize title=randomizeTitle}}{{/if}}{{#if searchControl}} {{> "stonetop.tab-search-control" title=searchTitle placeholder=searchPlaceholder}}{{/if}}{{#if collapse}}{{> "stonetop.section-collapse" collapse=collapse}}{{/if}}{{#if caret}}<i class="fas fa-caret-down stonetop-section-caret" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{/if}}</h3>
